An entry point that turns its helpers' errors into a result, as the style
guide's raise doctrine asks. `RequireSample` reports failure only by
raising, so its `/*@private;` is the annotation the convention requires and
gets no visibility_annotation_usage note (issue #371). `FormatId` raises
nothing and `TryRequire` catches its own raise, so their annotations are
the ones the convention would rather not see.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Main;
:PARAMETERS sSampleId;
:TRY;
DoProc("RequireSample", {sSampleId});
:CATCH;
ClearLastSSLError();
:RETURN {.F., "A sample is required."};
:ENDTRY;
:RETURN {.T., DoProc("FormatId", {sSampleId})};
:ENDPROC;

/*@private;
:PROCEDURE RequireSample;
:PARAMETERS sSampleId;
:IF Empty(sSampleId);
RaiseError("A sample is required");
:ENDIF;
:ENDPROC;

/*@private;
:PROCEDURE FormatId;
:PARAMETERS sSampleId;
:RETURN Upper(AllTrim(sSampleId));
:ENDPROC;

/*@private;
:PROCEDURE TryRequire;
:PARAMETERS sSampleId;
:TRY;
:IF Empty(sSampleId);
RaiseError("A sample is required");
:ENDIF;
:CATCH;
ClearLastSSLError();
:RETURN .F.;
:ENDTRY;
:RETURN .T.;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Main;
	:PARAMETERS sSampleId;

	:TRY;
		DoProc("RequireSample", {sSampleId});
	:CATCH;
		ClearLastSSLError();
		:RETURN {.F., "A sample is required."};
	:ENDTRY;

	:RETURN {.T., DoProc("FormatId", {sSampleId})};
:ENDPROC;

/*@private;
:PROCEDURE RequireSample;
	:PARAMETERS sSampleId;

	:IF Empty(sSampleId);
		RaiseError("A sample is required");
	:ENDIF;
:ENDPROC;

/*@private;
:PROCEDURE FormatId;
	:PARAMETERS sSampleId;

	:RETURN Upper(AllTrim(sSampleId));
:ENDPROC;

/*@private;
:PROCEDURE TryRequire;
	:PARAMETERS sSampleId;

	:TRY;
		:IF Empty(sSampleId);
			RaiseError("A sample is required");
		:ENDIF;
	:CATCH;
		ClearLastSSLError();
		:RETURN .F.;
	:ENDTRY;

	:RETURN .T.;
:ENDPROC;
